{{!-- Faith Received — the Desk workspace.

     Write with the library beside you: papers on the left, the draft in
     the middle, everything you have kept on the right, and a rail whose
     whole point is that a passage arrives WITH its citation rather than
     as loose text to be attributed later. Bound by
     assets/js/page/faith-desk.js.

     PORTED from the corpus owner's /desk. The shape is his. His chrome
     is not: no second masthead, no bridge bar, no Google fonts, no
     inline :root palette.

     SELF-CONTAINED. Like _bookmarks-panel.hbs and unlike _ask-panel.hbs,
     this partial ships its own .research-workspace wrapper and its own
     <script> tags, so it can be dropped into a tab shell whose template
     is owned by someone else. A host page that ALSO loads
     js/page/faith-desk.js is harmless: the script marks
     [data-desk-root] with data-desk-bound and returns on a second run.
     The three stores are plain window.MOFaith* definitions and are safe
     to define twice; the Notebook and Compare panels of the Research
     page load two of the same three.

     IT CREATES NOTHING UNTIL ITS TAB IS OPENED. Booting this panel
     writes to localStorage — with no papers yet it makes one, so that
     the reader lands in something they can type into rather than in an
     empty screen with a button. That is right on a page someone chose
     to open and wrong behind a tab they did not, where it would mean
     every visitor to the Research page silently acquired an untitled
     paper. So faith-desk.js waits on the `hidden` attribute of its
     [data-research-panel] host. See that file's "Waking up" section.

     WHAT IS NOT HERE. His rail has four tabs — notes, highlights,
     reading history, Ask conversations. Only the first has a store on
     our side; `fr_hl`, `fr_lastread` and `fr_chats` are his. Three tabs
     that were always empty would tell a reader they had highlighted
     nothing when they had highlighted plenty in a different tool. His
     iframe preview of a source beside the draft is gone too: a link
     that opens the reader in a new tab does the same work without
     putting our own pages in a frame.

     WHERE A DRAFT COMES FROM. Two ways in. The reader presses New paper
     here, or Compare sends one: its "Send to the Desk" writes a draft
     through window.MOFaithDesk and asks for this tab, with ?doc=<id> on
     the address. Same store, no integration between the two beyond it.
     ?doc= is a query parameter and not part of the hash on purpose: the
     hash names the workspace, and a paper is a thing this workspace is
     showing rather than a workspace of its own.

     A PAPER KNOWS ITS COLLECTION, so the rail opens on the material
     that paper is being written from. It is a default and never a
     constraint, and a collection since deleted degrades to everything
     rather than to an empty rail.

     DOM contract for assets/js/page/faith-desk.js. Every selector in
     that file:
       - [data-desk-root] wrapping everything
       - [data-desk-title], [data-desk-editor], [data-desk-words],
         [data-desk-savestate], [data-desk-toolbar] with
         [data-desk-cmd] / [data-desk-value] buttons
       - [data-desk-docs] holding [data-desk-doc-list],
         [data-desk-docs-close], [data-desk-new]; toggled by
         [data-desk-docs-toggle]
       - [data-desk-rail] holding [data-desk-collection],
         [data-desk-rail-search], [data-desk-rail-body],
         [data-desk-rail-more], [data-desk-rail-close]; toggled by
         [data-desk-rail-toggle]
       - [data-desk-scrim], [data-desk-status]
       - [data-desk-export], [data-desk-print], [data-desk-delete]

     THE TWO RAILS ARE DISCLOSURES. Both toggles carry aria-expanded and
     aria-controls, both panels can be closed from inside, and Escape
     closes them; below 1160px they overlay the draft rather than
     squeezing it, because the draft is what the page is for. --}}
<div class="research-workspace">
  <div class="desk" data-desk-root>

    {{!-- One line, and the lede kept to a sentence. Every pixel here is
          a pixel the draft does not get, and unlike the other panels
          this one has real chrome of its own immediately below. --}}
    <header class="rpanel-head rpanel-head--tight">
      <h2 class="rpanel-title">Desk</h2>
      <p class="rpanel-lede">Write with the library beside you. Anything you have kept goes into the draft with its citation already attached.</p>
    </header>

    {{!-- The bar. The two rail toggles bracket the title, so on a
          phone the two things that open are at the two thumbs. --}}
    <div class="desk-bar">
      <button type="button" class="desk-toggle" data-desk-docs-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="desk-docs">Papers</button>

      <label class="desk-title-field">
        <span class="visually-hidden">Title of this paper</span>
        <input type="text" class="desk-title" data-desk-title maxlength="160" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Untitled paper" />
      </label>

      <span class="desk-words" data-desk-words></span>
      <button type="button" class="desk-toggle" data-desk-rail-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="desk-rail">Research</button>
    </div>

    <p class="desk-status" data-desk-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

    <div class="desk-body">

      {{!-- Papers ────────────────────────────────────────── --}}
      <aside class="desk-panel desk-docs" id="desk-docs" data-desk-docs>
        <div class="desk-panel-head">
          <h2 class="desk-panel-title">Your papers</h2>
          <button type="button" class="desk-panel-close" data-desk-docs-close aria-label="Close your papers">Close</button>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="desk-act desk-act-primary" data-desk-new>New paper</button>
        <div class="desk-doc-list" data-desk-doc-list></div>
        <div class="desk-panel-foot">
          <button type="button" class="desk-act" data-desk-export>Download Markdown</button>
          <button type="button" class="desk-act" data-desk-print>Print or save PDF</button>
          <button type="button" class="desk-act desk-act-danger" data-desk-delete>Delete paper</button>
        </div>
      </aside>

      {{!-- The draft ─────────────────────────────────────── --}}
      <section class="desk-editor-wrap">
        <div class="desk-toolbar" data-desk-toolbar role="toolbar" aria-label="Formatting">
          <button type="button" class="desk-tool" data-desk-cmd="formatBlock" data-desk-value="h2" title="Section heading">H2</button>
          <button type="button" class="desk-tool" data-desk-cmd="formatBlock" data-desk-value="h3" title="Subheading">H3</button>
          <button type="button" class="desk-tool" data-desk-cmd="bold" title="Bold"><strong>B</strong></button>
          <button type="button" class="desk-tool" data-desk-cmd="italic" title="Italic"><em>I</em></button>
          <button type="button" class="desk-tool" data-desk-cmd="formatBlock" data-desk-value="blockquote" title="Block quotation">Quote</button>
          <button type="button" class="desk-tool" data-desk-cmd="insertUnorderedList" title="Bulleted list">List</button>
          <button type="button" class="desk-tool" data-desk-cmd="removeFormat" title="Clear formatting">Clear</button>
        </div>

        <div
          class="desk-editor"
          data-desk-editor
          contenteditable="true"
          spellcheck="true"
          role="textbox"
          aria-multiline="true"
          aria-label="The text of this paper"
        ></div>

        <p class="desk-savestate" data-desk-savestate role="status" aria-live="polite">Saved in this browser</p>
      </section>

      {{!-- Research ──────────────────────────────────────── --}}
      <aside class="desk-panel desk-rail" id="desk-rail" data-desk-rail>
        <div class="desk-panel-head">
          <h2 class="desk-panel-title">Your research</h2>
          <button type="button" class="desk-panel-close" data-desk-rail-close aria-label="Close your research">Close</button>
        </div>

        <label class="desk-field">
          <span class="desk-field-label">Show</span>
          <select class="desk-select" data-desk-collection></select>
        </label>

        <label class="desk-field">
          <span class="desk-field-label">Search what you have kept</span>
          <input type="search" class="desk-input" data-desk-rail-search maxlength="120" autocomplete="off" placeholder="A passage, a work, a note&hellip;" />
        </label>

        <div class="desk-rail-body" data-desk-rail-body></div>
        <button type="button" class="desk-act" data-desk-rail-more hidden>Show more</button>

        {{!-- Collections are the Notebook tab's own apparatus, so these
              are in-page links to sibling workspaces rather than
              navigations off this page. faith-desk.js re-points them at
              the tab strip when this panel is hosted; the markup
              carries the standalone URLs so they are correct with no
              script at all. --}}
        <p class="desk-panel-note"><a href="/the-faith-received/research/#notebook" data-desk-goto="notebook">Manage your collections</a> &middot; <a href="/the-faith-received/search/">Find more sources</a></p>
      </aside>

    </div>

    {{!-- The overlay backdrop for the two rails below 1160px. A
          real button so it is reachable by keyboard, though
          Escape is the usual way out. --}}
    <button type="button" class="desk-scrim" data-desk-scrim hidden aria-label="Close the open panel"></button>

    <p class="desk-foot-note">Papers are kept in this browser. They do not follow you to another device, and clearing site data clears them. Download anything you mean to keep.</p>

  </div>
</div>

{{!-- Last inside the panel on purpose: a non-visual node placed first
      would take the :first-child margin reset off the header above it.
      The notebook store first (the rail reads it), then collections
      (which reads MOFaithNotebook.RELATIONS), then the Desk's own
      store, then the page script, which needs all three. Page-template
      scripts run BEFORE site.min.js (FRONTEND §6.18); the only bundle
      global any of these touches is window.MOSafeHref, which ships in
      boot.min.js in <head>. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/lib/faith-notebook-store.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/lib/faith-collections-store.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/lib/faith-desk-store.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/page/faith-desk.js"}}"></script>
